[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] Fixes #514
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] ## Summary
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] - Replaces the renderer's all-or-nothing desktop grant with persisted per-tool grants for `http_fetch`, `url_navigate`, `eval_js`, `read_local_file`, `code_exec`, and `shell`.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] - Adds a one-time Agent/Full Auto onboarding system message with the same grant/decline panel used in the desktop sidebar.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] - Adds Agent-mode per-command shell approve/deny prompts; Full Auto skips the command prompt but still routes through the per-tool grant gate.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] - Extends router and e2e coverage for default-deny, partial grants, command denial, command approval, and Full Auto gating.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] ## Reproduce / Verify
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 1. Open the app with the desktop bridge available.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 2. Switch to Agent mode and grant only `shell` in the permission panel.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 3. Send `run \`ls ~\` in terminal`.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 4. Agent mode shows an approve/deny prompt and does not invoke the shell until approval.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 5. Switch to Full Auto with `shell` granted and send the same prompt; it runs without a per-command prompt. Ungranted tools still return a refusal.
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] ## Screenshot
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] ![Issue 514 per-tool permissions](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-514-693376bc3c68/docs/screenshots/issue-514-per-tool-permissions.png?raw=true)
[2026-06-18T07:08:21.503Z] [INFO] 
